    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1116">

                <pb facs="1466" n="1456" xml:id="pg1456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1121 McMillan, Archibald/8–3045:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-30T10:00:00+07:00">August 30, 1945—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 31—11:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1469. McMillan informed Embassy today that some time ago Supreme Court rules [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">ruled</hi>] that previous decisions in his case were
                    incorrect and sent case back to Szechuan high court for retrial. Case was
                    retried in high court here August 22 and court’s decision was announced August
                    28, [it] reversed previous decisions and rendered verdict of not guilty.</p>
                <p>New part of developments and copy of high court’s decision will be forwarded air
                        mail.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d1116-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
